{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "EvapOperatingModeDistribution",
    "description": "Steps E1-E3 of the process-evap-leaks chain: the operating-mode distribution the three evaporative calculators read. Ports docs/evap-leaks.md §2.3, joins K2-K7, and crates/moves-calculators/src/generators/evap_op_mode_distribution.rs:350 (stage 1) and :443 (stages 2 and 3) -- the port of EvaporativeEmissionsOperatingModeDistributionGenerator.java.\n\nWHAT IT COMPUTES, IN ONE LINE EACH. E1: `fractionOfOperating = least(1, SUM(SHO)/SUM(sourceHours))` per (hourDay, sourceType), both sums over the age dimension. E2: each soak mode takes `soakActivityFraction x (1 - fractionOfOperating)`. E3: operating mode 300 takes `greatest(0, 1 - SUM(soak shares))`.\n\nWHY THIS COMPONENT DECIDES THE WHOLE SLICE. `soakActivityFraction` is TankTemperatureGenerator's TTG-6 output, and TTG-1b is a quarter-hour recurrence the format cannot express (finding F12). This chain nevertheless needs nothing from it, because at an ON-NETWORK link `SourceHours = SHO` row for row (allocation.rs:631-682), so E1's numerator and denominator are the SAME COLUMN, the ratio is exactly 1, and E2's weight is exactly 0. The fixture's link is road type 4. That is why docs/evap-leaks.md §0.3 chose evap fuel leaks over permeation and FVV, and it is why rows 1 and 2 of `act_shoTotal` and `act_sourceHoursTotal` below carry the same two numbers: the ratio does not depend on what they are.\n\nTHE ZERO IS COMPUTED, NOT ASSUMED, and that distinction is the reason this file exists as a component rather than as a constant. This repository's characteristic failure is a plausible wrong value -- usually 0 -- on a document that validates cleanly (README.md; six instances on record). A document that wrote `opModeFraction[300] = 1` would agree with the snapshot on every one of its six rows and would be wrong the first time it met an off-network link.\n\nFOUR ROWS, TWO OF WHICH ARE PROBES, and this is the technique docs/esm-conventions.md §16.4 established after finding F19 removed the parameter-override one. Rows 1 and 2 are the fixture's own hourDayIDs 72 and 75 with the §6.0 activity sums. Rows 3 and 4 are the same two day types one hour earlier -- hourDayIDs 62 and 65, real MOVES keys this run does not select -- carrying CONSTRUCTED totals so that the two arms this fixture cannot reach are reachable: row 3's ratio is 300/500 = 0.6, which brings the soak modes alive, and row 4's is 625/500 = 1.25, which is the only place `least(1, .)` does anything. Nothing in rows 3 and 4 is claimed to be MOVES output; their soak fractions are the fixture's own, so only the operating share differs.\n\nMODE 300 IS A RESIDUAL, NOT `fractionOfOperating`. On rows 1, 2 and 4 the two are equal to the last bit. On row 3 the residual is 0.599999932 and `fractionOfOperating` is 0.6, because the snapshot's soak pair sums to 1.00000017 rather than to 1 -- six-significant-figure storage. A 6.8e-08 difference is the only thing in this fixture that distinguishes the right expression from a wrong one, so it is asserted.\n\nWHY `omd_opModeID` IS A PLAIN `const` AND `omd_hourDayID` IS BUILT FROM `enums`. A makearray region addresses ONE contiguous range per dimension per value (docs/esm-conventions.md §16.2), so a PRODUCT relation -- here 4 hour-days x 3 operating modes -- can build at most one of its two key columns from `enums`, whichever one the row order makes contiguous. The rows are hour-day-major, so `omd_hourDayID` is four contiguous blocks built as `hourID x 10 + dayID` from the `hour` and `day_type` enums, and `omd_opModeID` is the operating-mode column `opmodepolprocassoc` itself carries, as data. The `operating_mode` enums are still declared and are still what `assoc_opModeID` is built from, where each value does occupy one row.\n\nE3'S BRANCH IS A SEMI-JOIN, NOT A TEST ON THE MODE. `omd_hasSoakRow` asks whether `soakActivityFraction` carries a row for this (hourDay, opMode). That is not a trick to avoid comparing against 300: it is the reference's own control flow. Stage 2 emits a row for each mode SoakActivityFraction carries; stage 3 emits the mode-300 row for whatever those left. `soakactivityfraction` carries 150 and 151 and never 300, so the semi-join and the mode identity coincide -- and the semi-join is the one that stays right if a future default database gives a third soak mode.\n\nData: `soak_soakActivityFraction` and the two activity sums are the snapshot's (docs/evap-leaks.md §6.0). `act_fractionOfOperating` is computed here; the snapshot's own `fractionofoperating` table stores 1.000000000000 twice and the oracle reproduces it to 0 absolute error.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "moves",
      "onroad",
      "evaporative",
      "operating-mode",
      "component"
    ]
  },
  "enums": {
    "pollutant": {
      "TotalGaseousHydrocarbons": 1
    },
    "process": {
      "EvapFuelLeaks": 13
    },
    "source_type": {
      "PassengerCar": 21
    },
    "hour": {
      "SevenAM": 7,
      "SixAM": 6
    },
    "day_type": {
      "Weekend": 2,
      "Weekday": 5
    },
    "operating_mode": {
      "HotSoaking": 150,
      "ColdSoaking": 151,
      "Operating": 300,
      "NotAssociatedWithEvap": 501
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "evap_activity_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 4
    },
    "soak_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 9
    },
    "opmode_assoc_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 3
    },
    "evap_pol_process_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 1
    },
    "opmode_dist_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 12
    }
  },
  "coordinates": {
    "evap_omd_hour_day": {
      "source": "omd_hourDayID",
      "standard_name": "moves_hour_day_identifier"
    },
    "evap_omd_op_mode": {
      "source": "omd_opModeID",
      "standard_name": "moves_operating_mode_identifier"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "EvapOperatingModeDistribution": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../lib/evaporative.esm",
          "only": [
            "operating_share_of_activity",
            "soak_share"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ref": "../lib/identifiers.esm",
          "only": [
            "pol_process_id"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-12
      },
      "variables": {
        "runPolProcessID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "evap_pol_process_rows"
          ],
          "description": "K6's right-hand side: the run's pollutant-process, 100 x 1 + 13 = 113, built by `pol_process_id`. A one-row RELATION and not a scalar, because a join key column must resolve to a loop index of the aggregate (docs/esm-conventions.md §16.1) -- the build refuses a scalar there by name."
        },
        "act_hourDayID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "evap_activity_rows"
          ],
          "description": "E1's group key. 72 and 75 are the fixture's (hour 7, days 2 and 5); 62 and 65 are the probe rows of the description, one hour earlier."
        },
        "act_shoTotal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "evap_activity_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "K2: SUM(SHO) over the 41 ages, in hours. Rows 1-2 are the snapshot's own totals (docs/evap-leaks.md §6.0), 594.229522 h and 5654.364 h. Rows 3-4 are constructed: 300 and 625 against a denominator of 500, giving ratios 0.6 and 1.25."
        },
        "act_sourceHoursTotal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "evap_activity_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "K3: SUM(sourceHours) over the same ages. On rows 1-2 this is the SAME COLUMN as `act_shoTotal` -- A10's row-wise identity at an on-network link -- which is what makes the ratio exactly 1 rather than approximately 1."
        },
        "act_fractionOfOperating": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "evap_activity_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "E1, evap_op_mode_distribution.rs:350: `least(1, SUM(SHO)/SUM(sourceHours))` with the zero-denominator guard. 1, 1, 0.6, 1 -- the fourth being 1.25 capped."
        },
        "assoc_opModeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "opmode_assoc_rows"
          ],
          "description": "opmodepolprocassoc.opModeID for polProcessID 113: 150 (hot soaking), 151 (cold soaking), 300 (operating). Built from `enums`, which is possible here and not in `omd_opModeID` because each value occupies one row. The table's other 24 rows carry polProcessID -1 and K6 never admits them."
        },
        "assoc_polProcessID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "opmode_assoc_rows"
          ],
          "description": "opmodepolprocassoc.polProcessID, 113 on all three rows."
        },
        "soak_hourDayID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "soak_rows"
          ],
          "description": "soakactivityfraction.hourDayID. Rows are OPERATING-MODE-major -- 150, then 151, then the row-9 probe -- so this column is the one carried as data and `soak_opModeID` is the one built from `enums` (docs/esm-conventions.md §16.2; see the description)."
        },
        "soak_opModeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "soak_rows"
          ],
          "description": "soakactivityfraction.opModeID: 150 on rows 1-4, 151 on rows 5-8. Row 9 is a PROBE carrying operating mode 501, which opmodepolprocassoc lists only at polProcessID -1 -- a drive-cycle mode, not an evaporative one. It is the negative arm of the K5/K6 semi-join, and it sits on hourDayID 62 so that admitting it wrongly would change a non-zero number."
        },
        "soak_soakActivityFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "soak_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "soakactivityfraction[21, 261610, 8, hourDay, opMode].soakActivityFraction, TTG-6's output and the one F12-blocked quantity this chain touches. 0.00668717 / 0.993313 at hourDay 72 and 0.0221274 / 0.977873 at 75; the probe hour-days 62 and 65 reuse the same two splits, so only the operating share differs between a fixture row and its probe. The pair sums to 1.00000017, not 1. Row 9 carries 0.5 -- deliberately large, so that the semi-join failing to exclude it would move omd_soakSum for hourDay 62 from 0.400000068 to 0.600000068 and the residual from 0.599999932 to 0.399999932."
        },
        "soak_isAdmitted": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "soak_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "K5 and K6 as one semi-join under `bool_and_or` with a numeric body (docs/esm-conventions.md §3): does opmodepolprocassoc carry this operating mode for the run's pollutant-process? 1 on rows 1-8 and 0 on the row-9 probe, whose mode 501 the table carries only at polProcessID -1."
        },
        "soak_operatingShare": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "soak_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "K4: `act_fractionOfOperating` brought to each soak row on hourDayID. One clause, one pair -- the generator's join is on (sourceTypeID, hourDayID) and this component has one source type, so the second pair is the run scope and not a column."
        },
        "soak_opModeFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "soak_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "E2, :443 stage 2: `soak_share(soakActivityFraction, fractionOfOperating)` gated by the admission semi-join. Zero on the six rows whose operating share is 1, which is the whole fixture; 0.0026748680000000004 and 0.39732520000000005 on the two probe rows at share 0.6."
        },
        "omd_hourDayID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "opmode_dist_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The output relation's hour-day key, four contiguous blocks of three, built as `hourID x 10 + dayID` from the `hour` and `day_type` enums."
        },
        "omd_opModeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "opmode_dist_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The output relation's operating-mode key, 150 / 151 / 300 within each hour-day block. Carried as data rather than built from `enums` because a product relation can make only one of its two key columns contiguous (§16.2); see the description."
        },
        "omd_hasSoakRow": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "opmode_dist_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Semi-join to `soakactivityfraction` on (hourDayID, opModeID), gated by admission: is this a stage-2 row or a stage-3 row? 1 for the soak modes, 0 for mode 300. This is the reference's control flow and not a test on the identifier 300 -- stage 2 emits a row per mode SoakActivityFraction carries, stage 3 emits the residual row."
        },
        "omd_soakValue": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "opmode_dist_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The stage-2 fraction brought to this row on (hourDayID, opModeID). Zero on the mode-300 rows because no soak row matches -- an unmatched row contributes the additive identity (docs/esm-conventions.md §3)."
        },
        "omd_soakSum": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "opmode_dist_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "K7: SUM of the stage-2 fractions over this hour-day, which is E3's `SUM(opModeFraction)`. Joined on hourDayID ALONE, which is what makes it a group total rather than the row's own value -- the difference between this and `omd_soakValue` is one key pair."
        },
        "omd_opModeFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "opmode_dist_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "E2 and E3 together: the stage-2 fraction where a soak row exists, otherwise `greatest(0, 1 - omd_soakSum)`. This is the `opmodedistributiontemp` table, and the oracle reproduces its six fixture rows to 0 absolute error."
        }
      },
